WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.190
- Say hi to Kit Hoover,
have y'all met before?

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:02.023
- Hi.
- Hello.

00:00:02.023 --> 00:00:04.430
- We have never met but I
loved you on "Succession."

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:05.370
- Oh thank you, thank you.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.840
- Nice to meet you, so where
are you from originally?

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.673
We're both Southern.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.670
- I am originally from Arkansas Central.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:10.503
- [Kelly] Oh you're Southern?

00:00:10.503 --> 00:00:11.810
- Yeah, yeah,
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:12.643
- Arkansas people?

00:00:12.643 --> 00:00:13.476
- [Kelly] Arkansas.

00:00:13.476 --> 00:00:15.389
- Yeah, where from?
Where from?

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:16.222
- Jonesboro.

00:00:16.222 --> 00:00:17.085
- [Justin] Jonesboro.

00:00:17.085 --> 00:00:17.918
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:17.918 --> 00:00:18.751
- Atkins, Arkansas.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:21.860
And I grew up on a farm
out there in farm country,

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.357
one of the few black
farming families out there.

00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:26.190
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.220
- And did all types of things,

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.117
raised cows, chickens, hogs, and--

00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:30.920
- [Kelly] You're like a cowboy.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.080
- [Justin] Pretty much, pretty much.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.070
- Okay.
- Rode horses every weekend.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.830
My dad would come in and we
knew that we'd have to go out

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.120
and catch cows and take them to the sale.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.377
My dad would come in and
he'd say very declaratively,

00:00:41.377 --> 00:00:43.490
"Boys," 'cause I had two older brothers.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.544
He'd go, "Boys," we'd all go, "Ahhh!"

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:47.627
And we'd have to go out and
we'd have to catch cows and--

00:00:47.627 --> 00:00:48.460
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.293
- Ride horses and ride four wheelers

00:00:49.293 --> 00:00:50.126
and take them to the sale.

00:00:50.126 --> 00:00:51.315
- Now riding a four wheeler is fun man.

00:00:51.315 --> 00:00:52.640
(Justin laughs)
That's not a task.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.820
That's fun.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.760
And not when you're
working I guess, but you...

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.370
Were you ever on a farm?

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.346
- No, but I'm thinking--

00:00:57.346 --> 00:00:58.179
- [Kelly] Any farm skills?

00:00:58.179 --> 00:00:59.160
- Did you ever fall in love with the cows

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.930
and not wanna take 'em to town?

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.800
- Sometimes, sometimes, but--

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.202
- I would Charlotte Web that stuff.

00:01:04.202 --> 00:01:06.770
(all laughing)

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.210
- I think when you grow
up around it though,

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.250
'cause I grew up in front of the...

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.060
It's almost a compartmentalization
'cause it's like...

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.210
'Cause then my friends that
did do that growing up,

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.043
they'd be like,

00:01:15.043 --> 00:01:16.440
"Do you like your leather
seats in your car?"

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.395
- [Kit] Good call.

00:01:17.395 --> 00:01:18.228
- Yeah.

00:01:18.228 --> 00:01:19.420
'Cause it's working, it's a living.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.340
- It depends on where you're
from and how you grow up.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.230
But I also would do that.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.130
I'd be like, "why are you do...

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.480
I would never be able to do it myself,

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.480
but I understand why people do it.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.150
But how did you end up acting,

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.140
'cause that's kind of a different...

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.001
- Right.

00:01:30.001 --> 00:01:30.834
- [Kelly] Did you like drama
in school or something?

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:31.971
- Right.

00:01:31.971 --> 00:01:36.360
So in line with the whole
farming situation...

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.850
But we would be kind of cutting
hay during the summertimes

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:40.810
and we'd be on a tractor.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.240
Me and my older brothers
would be on a tractor

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.850
for like 12 hours at a time.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:44.683
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:44.683 --> 00:01:46.110
- And then we'd be
going kind of stir-crazy

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.050
in the heat and the bugs and everything,

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.810
and then I would have to
create stories in my brain

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:53.850
to entertain myself

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.260
and not go kind of have this manic,

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:57.308
weird episode on a tractor.

00:01:57.308 --> 00:01:58.180
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.080
- And so I would create
these sci-fi epics,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.280
these really weird period dramas,

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.527
and then as I graduated
high school, I was like,

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.520
"I think I can do something with this."

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.310
And I went to the University of Arkansas

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.750
and I got my BA there.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.500
I studied two years as a business major

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.000
and then a professor there said that

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.010
Juilliard was starting a graduate program

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:23.530
and that I should apply, and
I messed around and got in.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.260
- [Kelly] Gosh, that's amazing!

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.093
- [Kit] Huge.

00:02:26.093 --> 00:02:27.610
- [Kelly] I love that he saw that in you.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.370
Or the professor she or he,
I didn't know what it was,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.490
but I just mean that's amazing

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:31.681
the professor saw that in you.

00:02:31.681 --> 00:02:32.514
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:32.514 --> 00:02:33.347
- Yeah.

00:02:33.347 --> 00:02:36.950
Well staying on a tractor for a long time

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.570
did not prepare you for being
in the desert for a long time.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.000
Because I did see you post something

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.620
that I thought was awesome.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.453
Watch this.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:48.470
- It is a 105 degrees outside.
I got the air conditioner on

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:50.040
and I'm still hot.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.950
The back of my neck is hot.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.880
I don't even know where that comes from.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.853
Now I'm coming up on a ridge,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.373
if I get over this damn ridge,

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:05.250
best not be no more damn desert.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.793
How the desert this damn big?

00:03:08.617 --> 00:03:09.450
- [Kit] Yes!

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.283
(all laughing)
(audience applauding)

00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:13.230
- So I don't even think I have to ask you

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.200
where you're driving,

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.670
'cause I've driven from Texas
to California many a times,

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.690
and there is a stretch,

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:19.790
is that where you were kinda coming from,

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:20.623
Arkansas to California?

00:03:20.623 --> 00:03:21.456
- Yeah.

00:03:21.456 --> 00:03:22.970
It was Flagstaff to California.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.660
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.670
There's one thing, if
you don't stop for gas...

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.503
- Yeah.

00:03:27.503 --> 00:03:28.356
I stopped for...

00:03:28.356 --> 00:03:29.439
Well I have a really cool hybrid car,

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:30.570
so I only stopped for gas three times.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.561
- [Kelly] Oh that's awesome.

00:03:31.561 --> 00:03:32.744
Yeah.

00:03:32.744 --> 00:03:34.480
- But yeah, I stopped
for gas in the desert

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.870
and that's after that video.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.660
I was like, "It is so hot out here."

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:38.493
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:38.493 --> 00:03:40.010
- I don't know what's going on.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:41.210
I drove from Arkansas,

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:42.290
picked up the car in Arkansas

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:44.510
and I drove from Arkansas to Los Angeles,

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.730
and I was driving out here to
do the show, do "Grand Crew."

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.444
- Oh my gosh, that's so awesome.

00:03:49.444 --> 00:03:50.310
(audience clapping)

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.143
That's so very cool.

00:03:51.143 --> 00:03:54.210
So did you swear off road
trips from "Road Rules."

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.550
Were you just like done?

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:56.383
Were you...

00:03:56.383 --> 00:03:57.808
- I like to get neked in
a hot tub (indistinct)

00:03:57.808 --> 00:03:58.827
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:58.827 --> 00:03:59.660
- [Justin] I saw that.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:00.493
- Don't worry about it Justin.

00:04:00.493 --> 00:04:01.326
- ]Justin] I saw that.

00:04:01.326 --> 00:04:02.430
- Do you say "neked?"

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.990
- I say "naked."

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:05.823
- [Kit] Oh!

00:04:05.823 --> 00:04:07.470
- See I think that sounds more hillbilly.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.130
- If you use it in a sentence,

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.440
I came in and he was "neked."

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.460
That's kind of country.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.150
If I came in and he was "naked."

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:15.983
Yeah, yeah you're right.

00:04:15.983 --> 00:04:17.532
- Exactly!
- You're right.

00:04:17.532 --> 00:04:19.279
- Exactly!
- You're right,

00:04:19.279 --> 00:04:20.229
- We win!

00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:21.062
- You right.

00:04:21.062 --> 00:04:22.303
(Kit and Kelly laughing)
(audience applauding)

00:04:22.303 --> 00:04:25.730
- I was like "That one
sounds more country to me."

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:26.640
You were like, "You know what?

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.585
Nevermind."

00:04:27.585 --> 00:04:28.418
- [Kit] Nevermind.

00:04:28.418 --> 00:04:29.251
(all laughing)

00:04:29.251 --> 00:04:30.084
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:04:30.084 --> 00:04:30.917
Wait, let's talk about your new show

00:04:30.917 --> 00:04:33.100
'cause we've had a couple
castmates on here already.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.310
So let's talk about "Grand Crew."

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:36.010
It returns post-Olympics this week,

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.040
so tell us about who you are in it.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.630
- Well "Grand Crew" is a
brand new comedy with NBC.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.180
It's a show about a group
of friends in Los Angeles,

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.840
and they meet regularly at a wine bar

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.010
to wind down as we say,

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:51.300
and they sort of explore
the cultural nuances

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.067
of their work life, their love life,

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:54.820
and their friendships with each other.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:57.490
And I play the character Wyatt,

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:59.580
who is the only married one of the group,

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.000
and he brings a sense of optimism

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.430
and curiosity to his friends
whenever they find themselves

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.930
in weird and awkward situations.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:07.763
- Yeah.

00:05:07.763 --> 00:05:09.497
- And yeah for me, it's been
great to get to explore that.

00:05:09.497 --> 00:05:10.660
- And it's funny

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.493
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:11.493 --> 00:05:12.540
- The show is funny.
We need to laugh.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:13.373
- [Kelly] We need to laugh.

00:05:13.373 --> 00:05:14.340
- Wait, what do your brothers do

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.630
since you're this established actor?

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.130
- Ooh, my oldest brother

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.880
is a marketing schemes
manager for Walmart.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:21.713
- [Kit] Nice.

00:05:21.713 --> 00:05:22.730
I Love Walmart.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:23.770
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.280
- And my second older
brother is an engineer

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.540
at a nuclear plant.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:28.500
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.020
- And a former Marine,
served two tours in Iraq.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:31.920
- Wow!

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.050
- And just had a new baby!

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.150
- So here's my question...

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.530
Oh that's so sweet!

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.183
I love baby smell.

00:05:37.183 --> 00:05:38.016
(Kit and Justin laughing)

00:05:38.016 --> 00:05:39.900
- So wait, so I just
went there in my head.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.500
So were your parents upset

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.370
that not one of you wanted
to do farming? (laughs)

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:46.670
- A little bit.

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:47.839
My father...

00:05:47.839 --> 00:05:49.040
(Kit and Kelly laughing)

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:49.873
A little bit--

00:05:49.873 --> 00:05:52.339
- He's like, "Seriously, not one of you?"

00:05:52.339 --> 00:05:53.172
- Yeah.

00:05:53.172 --> 00:05:54.005
- 'Cause I have a ranch and I'm like,

00:05:54.005 --> 00:05:56.176
"One of 'em better like it."

00:05:56.176 --> 00:05:57.009
It's like...

00:05:57.009 --> 00:05:59.760
- I mean I wanna go back and
I could have taken that route,

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.300
I could have got my own contract

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.112
with a corporation and did farming but--

00:06:04.112 --> 00:06:05.160
- Yeah you did what you love though.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.013
- Yeah, yeah.
- Its what I'd do.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.600
- They were kind of
hesitant to support me.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.433
- Yeah.

00:06:12.433 --> 00:06:14.580
- I think the day that
I got into Juilliard

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:16.283
I called him...

00:06:16.283 --> 00:06:17.367
I got off the plane, I
called him, I was like,

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:18.270
"I got in,"

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.040
And he goes, "Oh, that's good.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.170
Well call me if you need any money."

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.690
Click!
(audience laughs)

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.390
- I mean here's the thing,

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:27.680
if getting into Juilliard
doesn't impress your parents,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.587
there's nothing you can
do that will impress them.

00:06:29.587 --> 00:06:30.660
- No.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.230
- My brother had a
really different response

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:34.420
and I can't say it on television.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.550
(Kelly laughing)

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.570
- I wanna hear it in the commercial break.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:40.240
All right, thank you guys so much!

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.890
Everybody you can catch
"Grand Crew" Tuesdays on NBC.

